# no-fo.ttl — the no-FO baseline overlay (intentionally a no-op).
#
# [OPUS-4.8] FO-KM benchmark, Metric 1 (epic sq-mztg8). Design record:
# research/foundational-ontology-km-benchmark.md (PR #1106). 🤖 SPARQ agent.
#
# This is the INCUMBENT arm: the shipped PKG already types every instance directly
# (pkg:Task / pkg:Finding / pkg:Source / pkg:Technique) with parents to DOMAIN
# vocabularies (schema:Action, sig-impl:Assertion, fabio:Expression, skos:Concept) —
# it imports NO foundational/upper ontology (verified: `grep -ri gufo crates/sparq-kb`
# returns nothing). So the "no-FO" arm is the PKG with NO overlay loaded; this file
# adds NOTHING.
#
# It exists so the per-arm `pkg-query` command is uniform across arms (every arm passes
# exactly one `--extra-graph overlays/<arm>.ttl`), and so an FO-EXERCISING task that
# asks "which entities are perdurants/processes?" returns ZERO rows here (the no-FO arm
# genuinely lacks the foundational category) while an FO arm answers it — the
# discrimination the benchmark is built on.
#
# Deliberately empty (one harmless ontology-metadata triple only, so the file is valid
# non-empty Turtle that loads + closes cleanly under --close owl-rl).

@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix pkgfo: <https://sparq.dev/ns/pkg/fo#> .

pkgfo:no-fo-overlay a owl:Ontology ;
  rdfs:label "no-FO baseline overlay (no-op)"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "Adds no foundational typing — the shipped-PKG incumbent arm."@en-GB .
